<div>
  <h1>About This Project</h1>
  <p>
    Welcome to my Brewery App! This website helps you browse and explore different breweries across the United States.
  </p>

  <h2>Where the Data Comes From</h2>
  <p>
    All the information is pulled directly from a free public website called the <strong>Open Brewery DB API</strong>. It gives us real-world details like brewery names, cities, types, and websites.
  </p>

  <h2>How It Is Organized & ERD Summary</h2>
  <p>
    The database uses a <strong>One-to-Many (1:N) relationship</strong> built with two main tables:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>States:</strong> The parent table containing unique state records.</li>
    <li><strong>Breweries:</strong> The child table containing individual brewery details, linked via a foreign key (state_id).</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Because of this relationship, clicking on a state shows all its breweries, and clicking on a brewery shows its parent state details!
  </p>

  <div>
    <%= link_to "View States", states_path %> | 
    <%= link_to "View Breweries", breweries_path %>
  </div>
</div>